course: dictionary
lesson: 12810
title: Stretching words: elongate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Elongate means to make something longer, or to become longer. Look inside the word and you can see the word long. When something elongates, it gets longer, but it does not turn into a different thing.
explain: «As the sun sank, the shadows began to elongate.» The shadows did not move away. They got longer across the grass. When a shadow is longer than usual, we can call it elongated.
explain: Artists also use this word. «The painter drew tall, elongated figures.» Her people look thinner and taller than real people, because she stretched them on purpose. In maths, «The rectangle was an elongated shape» means it is stretched in one direction, so it is long rather than square.
fact: Elongate means to make something longer, or to become longer.
fact: Elongated is an adjective and means long and thin, longer than usual.
fact: The verb forms are elongate, elongates, elongated and elongating.
fact: In science, cells can elongate, and shadows can elongate when the sun is low.
fact: A good check is to swap in «make longer» or «stretched out» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «As the sun sank, the shadows began to elongate.» What does elongate mean? | To break into pieces | To make something shorter | *To make something longer | To change its colour
exercise: The artist drew «tall, elongated figures». What does elongated mean here? | Bright and shiny | Short and round | Wet and heavy | *Long and thin, longer than usual
exercise: «The rectangle was an elongated shape.» Find and copy the word that tells you the shape is stretched longer. | The | *elongated | was | shape
test: «The cell began to elongate before it divided.» What does elongate mean in this sentence? | To fall over | To stop moving | *To grow longer | To shrink to a dot
test: Which thing could be described as elongated? | A ball | A circle | A dot | *A long, thin rectangle
exam: «By evening the shadows had begun to elongate across the lawn.» What does elongate mean here? | To disappear | To turn black | To shrink | *To become longer
